{"id":"SEC-001","category":"security","criterion":"error_handling","severity":"HIGH","score":2,"file":"head/.claude/adapters/loa_cheval/providers/agy_headless_adapter.py","line":124,"code_snippet":"if not agy_opt_in_enabled():\n    raise AgyOptInRequiredError()","reasoning_trace":"AgyOptInRequiredError is a ConfigError (types.py:503); cheval.py:2544-2553 'except ChevalError' records error_class UNKNOWN, prints _error_json(code, message, retryable) and returns; _error_json (cheval.py:142-146) and ChevalError.to_json never serialise context, so failure_class opt_in_required is unreachable on the wire; every stock Google fallback_chain ends in google:gemini-headless (model-config.yaml:216,228,248,262,289); _companion_failure_class (adversarial-review.sh:2979-2995) has no opt_in_required class.","finding":"Opt-in refusal inside the chain walk hard-aborts with INVALID_CONFIG, masking the upstream Google HTTP failure and counting as a failed voice; the documented machine-readable failure_class seam is never emitted.","critique":"The 'never a failed voice' contract (types.py:503-510) holds only for planner-side filters, not for the catalog chain walk every stock Google chain takes.","remediation":"Catch AgyOptInRequiredError before the generic ChevalError arm: record OPT_IN_REQUIRED in models_failed, keep the previous hop's exception, continue; or drop gemini-headless from the resolved chain at plan time when the opt-in is off. Serialise failure_class in _error_json; teach _companion_failure_class the class; add a two-hop test.","confidence":"high","references":["CWE-755 https://cwe.mitre.org/data/definitions/755.html","CWE-392 https://cwe.mitre.org/data/definitions/392.html"]}
{"id":"SEC-002","category":"security","criterion":"authorization","severity":"MEDIUM","score":3,"file":"head/.claude/adapters/loa_cheval/config/loader.py","line":122,"code_snippet":"root = project_root or _find_project_root()\ntry:\n    merged = _deep_merge(load_system_defaults(root), load_project_config(root))","reasoning_trace":"The predicate merges the System-Zone catalog under the project config to read one key; a headless.agy_opt_in: true in .claude/defaults/model-config.yaml opts in without .loa.config.yaml; _find_project_root() runs outside the fail-closed try (Path.cwd() raises when the cwd vanished). Confirmed by DISS-C-002 and review Observation 2.","finding":"Opt-in authority surface is wider than documented (System-Zone layer, cwd walk) and root resolution escapes the fail-closed guard; both YAML files are re-parsed per call.","critique":"The control exists to keep the review diff off a world-readable argv; its authority should be exactly the project config.","remediation":"Read load_project_config(root) alone; move _find_project_root() inside the try; memoise per project_root.","confidence":"high","references":["CWE-15 https://cwe.mitre.org/data/definitions/15.html","CWE-214 https://cwe.mitre.org/data/definitions/214.html"]}
{"id":"SEC-003","category":"security","criterion":"confidentiality","severity":"MEDIUM","score":3,"file":"head/tools/ceiling-probe-live.py","line":217,"code_snippet":"env = {**os.environ, \"CLAUDE_CODE_DISABLE_AUTO_MEMORY\": \"1\"}","reasoning_trace":"Adapter contract 'never inherit subprocess env' via build_headless_subprocess_env() (providers/base.py:794-819) strips ANTHROPIC_API_KEY; the probe passes the full shell env while stamping host_route/cli_model from wrapper env vars, so provenance may describe a transport the measurement never used.","finding":"Probe forwards the shell's credentials to the CLI subprocess and may record Bedrock provenance for a direct-API measurement.","critique":"D-3.9 'the probe measures the shape the adapter dispatches' must include the environment.","remediation":"env = build_headless_subprocess_env(); env['CLAUDE_CODE_DISABLE_AUTO_MEMORY']='1'; refuse --transport claude-headless when ANTHROPIC_API_KEY is set.","confidence":"medium","references":["CWE-526 https://cwe.mitre.org/data/definitions/526.html","CWE-668 https://cwe.mitre.org/data/definitions/668.html"]}
{"id":"ARCH-002","category":"architecture","criterion":"resilience","severity":"MEDIUM","score":3,"file":"head/.claude/defaults/model-config.yaml","line":494,"code_snippet":"effective_input_ceiling: 936000   # cycle-124 FR-3 (SDD §2.1): see claude-fable-5-1","reasoning_trace":"transport: claude-headless, cli_model global.anthropic.claude-opus-5-5 (:510-512) on the HTTP anthropic entry; _lookup_max_input_tokens('anthropic', ...) reads it for direct-API callers; calibrated bounds are never lowered by observation (LSP-5); account_limits.itpm null.","finding":"A CLI/Bedrock measurement sets the direct-API entry's pre-emption bound; low-ITPM accounts lose the 180K pre-emption and 429 on the wire.","critique":"The entry's own reprobe_trigger admits the route gap.","remediation":"Per-transport ceiling or keep the HTTP entry at the policy cap until an --transport api probe; gate on account_limits.itpm when known.","confidence":"medium","references":["CWE-770 https://cwe.mitre.org/data/definitions/770.html"]}
{"id":"CQ-001","category":"code_quality","criterion":"test_coverage","severity":"MEDIUM","score":3,"file":"head/.claude/adapters/tests/test_anthropic_catalog_floor.py","line":146,"code_snippet":"cap = entry[\"effective_input_ceiling\"] if _measured(entry) else CEILING_CAP\nexpected = min(cap, entry[\"context_window\"] - _default_max_tokens(entry))","reasoning_trace":"For measured entries the equality reduces to eic <= cw - dmt, asserted on line 148; test_ceiling_probe_cli_transport.py:459 skips permanently now that the live catalog is calibrated.","finding":"Catalog floor test is tautological for measured entries; live-catalog writer layout has no coverage.","critique":"The sweep guards the invariant, not the measured value.","remediation":"Assert eic == min(measured_input_tokens, cw - dmt) and probed_ceiling == eic; replace the skip with a reset fixture.","confidence":"high","references":["CWE-1164 https://cwe.mitre.org/data/definitions/1164.html"]}
{"id":"ARCH-003","category":"architecture","criterion":"complexity","severity":"MEDIUM","score":3,"file":"head/tools/ceiling-probe-live.py","line":632,"code_snippet":"def _main_cli(args) -> int:","reasoning_trace":"_main_cli spans 632-847 with six closures over nonlocal samples/ratio/spent_micro; write_catalog_operator_set (402-480) is line-level YAML surgery with three nested finders; both exceed the 50-line threshold without a justification marker.","finding":"SIMPLICITY[shrink]: bisection and catalog writer are untestable below whole-run level.","critique":"Lift state into a dataclass; split the writer into three steps.","remediation":"Dataclass with step/next_target methods; 'replace scalars' / 'replace calibration block' / 'replace provenance comment' functions.","confidence":"high","references":["CWE-1120 https://cwe.mitre.org/data/definitions/1120.html"]}
{"id":"CQ-002","category":"code_quality","criterion":"documentation","severity":"LOW","score":4,"file":"head/.claude/data/schemas/model-config-v3.schema.json","line":306,"reasoning_trace":"Description says measured_input_tokens is 'the value written to probed_ceiling / effective_input_ceiling'; shipped entry 972887 vs 936000 after the I2 clamp.","finding":"Schema description contradicts the fr23b clamp.","remediation":"'the raw accepted size; probed/effective = min(this, context_window - default_max_tokens)'.","confidence":"high","references":["CWE-1059 https://cwe.mitre.org/data/definitions/1059.html"]}
{"id":"CQ-003","category":"code_quality","criterion":"documentation","severity":"LOW","score":4,"file":"head/.claude/adapters/cheval.py","line":2834,"reasoning_trace":"Comments at cheval.py:2834 and modelinv.py:498 list effort_source as caller | catalog | none; resolve_effort and the schema emit 'extra'. model-config.yaml:494 trailing comment is stale on a calibrated value and _set_scalar preserves it.","finding":"Stale comments on derived/calibrated values.","remediation":"Add 'extra' to both comments; drop the cycle-124 trailing comment on line 494.","confidence":"high","references":["CWE-1059 https://cwe.mitre.org/data/definitions/1059.html"]}
{"id":"CQ-004","category":"code_quality","criterion":"documentation","severity":"LOW","score":4,"file":"head/.claude/defaults/model-config.yaml","line":509,"reasoning_trace":"method: probed_headless on an entry the tool refused to write (outcome partial per :496); the tool writes probed_headless only on clean.","finding":"method field claims the tool's method on a hand-written value.","remediation":"Omit method or note the partial outcome in reprobe_trigger.","confidence":"high","references":["CWE-1059 https://cwe.mitre.org/data/definitions/1059.html"]}
{"id":"SEC-004","category":"security","criterion":"input_validation","severity":"LOW","score":4,"file":"head/.claude/adapters/cheval.py","line":912,"code_snippet":"if explicit:\n    return explicit, \"caller\"","reasoning_trace":"Caller rung bypasses _valid_effort (argparse trusted); extra rung is strip().lower()-normalised (:922) but params.default_effort is not; the 'both' WARN (:909) fires for HTTP entries whose extra.effort is never read. Confirmed by DISS-C-003.","finding":"Effort rungs validated unevenly at the declared chokepoint.","remediation":"Run every rung through _valid_effort; normalise both; warn only for CLI entries without a caller value.","confidence":"medium","references":["CWE-20 https://cwe.mitre.org/data/definitions/20.html"]}
{"id":"ARCH-004","category":"architecture","criterion":"standards","severity":"LOW","score":4,"file":"head/.claude/adapters/cheval.py","line":1519,"reasoning_trace":"resolve_effort runs once against the primary entry; the CompletionRequest rides every hop; effort_effective (:2838-2845) recomputed for final_model_id with the primary's value.","finding":"A fallback hop's own default_effort is never applied.","remediation":"Per-hop resolve or a documented decision in D-2.2.","confidence":"medium","references":["CWE-684 https://cwe.mitre.org/data/definitions/684.html"]}
{"id":"SEC-005","category":"security","criterion":"confidentiality","severity":"LOW","score":4,"file":"head/.claude/adapters/loa_cheval/providers/claude_headless_adapter.py","line":145,"code_snippet":"*([] if prompt is None else [prompt]),","reasoning_trace":"Public module-level builder accepts prompt= and places it after -p; both callers pass None; the cycle-126 fix moved the prompt to stdin to close /proc/<pid>/cmdline exposure. Confirmed by DISS-C-004.","finding":"build_headless_argv re-exposes the argv-prompt surface as a one-argument choice.","remediation":"Drop the prompt parameter or assert prompt is None with a comment naming the exposure.","confidence":"medium","references":["CWE-214 https://cwe.mitre.org/data/definitions/214.html"]}
{"id":"SEC-006","category":"security","criterion":"injection","severity":"LOW","score":4,"file":"head/tools/ceiling-probe-live.py","line":467,"reasoning_trace":"provenance f-string splices route (from --host-route) and cli_model (from --cli-model / ANTHROPIC_DEFAULT_*_MODEL) unquoted into a YAML comment line; scalars go through json.dumps and cli_version is first-line-only. DISS-C-005 partly refuted.","finding":"A newline in an operator string breaks out of the provenance comment into a catalog YAML line.","remediation":"Strip CR/LF from route and cli_model before formatting the comment.","confidence":"medium","references":["CWE-74 https://cwe.mitre.org/data/definitions/74.html"]}
{"id":"ARCH-005","category":"architecture","criterion":"modularity","severity":"LOW","score":4,"file":"head/.claude/adapters/loa_cheval/providers/agy_headless_adapter.py","line":124,"reasoning_trace":"Gate repeated in complete (:124), validate_config (:261), health_check (:295); HeadlessCLIAdapter has exactly those three public entry points (headless_cli.py:359,460,479), so no unguarded path today; DISS-C-001 premise partly refuted, design note kept.","finding":"Opt-in enforced per method rather than at one construction seam.","remediation":"Gate once in __init__/get_adapter or in HeadlessCLIAdapter._dispatch.","confidence":"high","references":["CWE-657 https://cwe.mitre.org/data/definitions/657.html"]}
{"id":"CQ-005","category":"code_quality","criterion":"readability","severity":"LOW","score":4,"file":"head/tools/ceiling-probe-live.py","line":261,"code_snippet":"cha.ClaudeHeadlessAdapter._raise_for_error(__import__(\"types\").SimpleNamespace(provider=\"claude-headless\"), ...)","reasoning_trace":"Instance method called with a fake self; any new self attribute lands in the except Exception arm as kind other. __import__('time')/('re') at module level (:135,:144,:148).","finding":"Fragile coupling to a private adapter method's use of self.","remediation":"Make _raise_for_error a staticmethod taking provider, or instantiate the adapter; use plain imports.","confidence":"high","references":["CWE-1061 https://cwe.mitre.org/data/definitions/1061.html"]}
{"id":"SEC-007","category":"security","criterion":"authorization","severity":"LOW","score":4,"file":"head/.claude/skills/bridgebuilder-review/resources/config.ts","line":176,"code_snippet":"return { optIn, mode: process.env.LOA_HEADLESS_MODE || mode || \"prefer-api\" };","reasoning_trace":"isAgyRouted treats every google voice as agy-routed under cli-only; multi-model-pipeline.ts:422 compares against models.length - notPlanned.length, so an env var removes configured voices from the merge quorum. Fail-closed for the opt-in itself; same precedence as cheval.","finding":"LOA_HEADLESS_MODE lowers the Bridgebuilder merge quorum without being named in the docs.","remediation":"Read mode from the config file only in Bridgebuilder, or log the env override with the not-planned line.","confidence":"low","references":["CWE-807 https://cwe.mitre.org/data/definitions/807.html"]}
